B.aW6=new A.at(B.pp,["open_camera","CAMERA TOOL: Open the camera for visual perception. Call this when the user asks visual questions.\n\n**When to use:**\n- 'Can you see [anything]?'\n- 'Look around' / 'What do you see?'\n- 'What's on the table?'\n- 'Can you see this [object]?'\n- 'What am I holding?'\n- 'Read this' / 'What does it say?'\n- 'How many [objects]?'\n- 'Open camera'\n\n**How it works:**\n1. You call this tool\n2. Camera starts streaming visual frames\n3. Tool waits ~4 seconds for frames to reach you\n4. Tool response includes instructions - FOLLOW THEM EXACTLY\n5. By the time you get the response, visual frames are already in your context\n\n**CRITICAL - Response Instructions:**\nThe tool response will tell you how to respond. Read it carefully and follow instructions:\n- If user asked a visual question: Analyze ACTUAL visual frames and answer truthfully\n- If user asked about object X but you don't see X: Say 'I don't see X. I see [what's actually there]'\n- NEVER say 'yes I can see X' unless X is truly visible in the frames\n- Base response on ACTUAL visual data, NOT on what user mentioned\n\n**Examples:**\n- User: 'Can you see water bottle?' -> Call open_camera -> Follow tool instructions -> Answer based on actual frames\n- If frames show bottle: 'Yes, I can see a water bottle'\n- If frames don't show bottle: 'I don't see a water bottle. I see a laptop and phone on the desk'\n\n**DO NOT USE `detect_and_highlight_object` unless user wants to HIGHLIGHT specific objects.**",B.Fn],t.EU)
B.a4e={type:0,properties:1,required:2}
B.a4c={query:0}
B.a4d={type:0,description:1}
B.aVX=new A.at(B.a4d,["string","The user's object detection request. Include what object to detect/highlight and any distinguishing features (e.g., 'highlight the blue tablet', 'which bottle is for cleaning?', 'detect the red cup')."],t.w)
B.aW2=new A.at(B.a4c,[B.aVX],t.vb)
B.UF=s(["query"],t.s)
B.aSf=new A.at(B.a4e,["object",B.aW2,B.UF],t.EU)
B.aW7=new A.at(B.pp,["detect_and_highlight_object","VISUAL DETECTION TOOL: Detect and visually highlight specific objects in the camera view. This tool freezes the camera, identifies the requested objects, and highlights them on screen with segmentation masks.\n\nCRITICAL: ONLY use when the user asks to HIGHLIGHT, DETECT, or DISTINGUISH specific objects. DO NOT use for general questions or descriptions.\n\nWHEN TO USE (must contain highlighting/detection intent):\n- 'Highlight [object]' / 'Detect [object]' / 'Find [object]'\n- 'Which one is [description]?' (e.g. 'which one is the charger?')\n- 'Point to [object]' / 'Identify the [specific object]'\n- Questions about SPECIFIC objects among many: 'which key is for the car?'\n\nDO NOT USE for (answer these verbally from the live camera frames already in your context):\n- General questions: 'What do you see?', 'What is this?', 'What's that?', 'What am I looking at?', 'Describe this'\n- Reading requests: 'Read this', 'What does it say?'\n- Scene descriptions or general observation: 'Look at this', 'Show me what you see'\n- Counting: 'How many X are there?'\n\nKEY DISTINCTION:\n- 'What do you see?' = general description -> DON'T use this tool, describe the scene verbally\n- 'Which one is the remote?' = specific object detection -> USE this tool",B.aSf],t.EU)
B.aVW=new A.at(B.a4d,["string","The full and unaltered user query related to travel, stay, booking, or location information. Pass exactly what the user asked, without rephrasing, summarizing, or modifying it."],t.w)
B.aW1=new A.at(B.a4c,[B.aVW],t.vb)
B.aSe=new A.at(B.a4e,["object",B.aW1,B.UF],t.EU)
B.aW8=new A.at(B.pp,["location_search","CRITICAL: This function MUST be called for ANY user queries related to travel, stay, or location-based information. The model must NEVER deny or say it cannot perform the task \u2014 it must ALWAYS pass the user's full query to this function instead.\n\nThis includes ANY query involving planning, finding, comparing, recommending, checking, exploring, or BOOKING \u2014 for hotels, restaurants, weather, flights, events, directions, or itineraries.\n\nThe model should not attempt to answer, explain, or reject the user's query \u2014 only forward it entirely to this function.\n\nExamples: 'Book a hotel in Delhi', 'Find a hotel near Connaught Place', 'Plan a trip to Japan for 7 days', 'Create an itinerary for Kerala', 'Find restaurants near CST station', 'Flights from Mumbai to Goa on Friday', 'Weather in Shimla next weekend', 'Events in Bangalore this weekend', 'Directions from Pune to Lonavala', etc.",B.aSe],t.EU)
B.aW9=new A.at(B.pp,["close_camera","CAMERA TOOL: Close the device camera when it is no longer needed. The voice call stays active.\n\n**WHEN TO USE:**\n- User asks to stop or close the camera\n- After finishing camera-based tasks to free system resources",B.Fn],t.EU)
B.aWa=new A.at(B.pp,["capture_camera_frame","CAMERA CAPTURE TOOL: Capture and save the current camera frame as an image. Use this when the user wants to take a picture or save the current view.\n\n**WHEN TO USE:**\n- User requests to capture/take a picture: 'capture this', 'take a picture', 'save this image'\n- User wants to save what the camera is currently seeing: 'save this view', 'capture the current frame'\n- User asks to take a photo: 'take a photo', 'snap a picture', 'can you capture this'\n\n**IMPORTANT: The camera (video mode) must already be open before using this tool. If it is not open, tell the user to open the camera first.**\n\n**EXAMPLES:**\n- User: 'Can you please capture this' -> capture_camera_frame()\n- User: 'Take a picture of this' -> capture_camera_frame()\n- User: 'Save this image' -> capture_camera_frame()\n- User: 'Capture the current frame' -> capture_camera_frame()\n- User: 'What do you see?' -> NOT a capture request, describe the live camera frames instead\n- User: 'Highlight the bottle' -> use detect_and_highlight_object instead",B.Fn],t.EU)
